      'Blackstone\'s real estate empire demonstrates the cardinal rule of real estate investing: the money is made at the purchase price, not the sale price. By buying during maximum distress at 40-60 cents on the dollar, using moderate leverage, and applying professional management, they turned a financial crisis into the largest real estate portfolio on Earth. For individual investors, the lesson is the same: buy when others are fearful, use conservative leverage, and think in decades, not quarters.'
