      'Watch the order of operations. Cap rate = Net Operating Income / Property Value. NOI is gross rent ($60K) minus operating expenses ($24K), which is $36K, not the full $60K. Then $36K / $600K = 6%. The mortgage payment never enters the cap rate, and you never divide by expenses.'
