        { term: 'Smart Contract', definition: 'Self-executing code stored on a blockchain that automatically enforces agreement terms when conditions are met. No intermediary needed. Pioneered by Ethereum.', example: 'A DeFi lending protocol uses smart contracts to automatically liquidate a borrower\'s collateral if it drops below 150% of the loan value, no human intervention required.' },
        { term: 'DeFi (Decentralized Finance)', definition: 'Financial services (lending, borrowing, trading, insurance) built on blockchain without traditional intermediaries like banks. Over $50 billion in total value locked (TVL).', example: 'Aave lets you earn 3-8% interest on stablecoins by lending them to borrowers, all through smart contracts, no bank takes a cut.' },
        { term: 'Market Cap (Crypto)', definition: 'The total value of a cryptocurrency = current price multiplied by circulating supply. Used to compare the relative size of different crypto assets.', example: 'Bitcoin at $70K with 19.5M coins in circulation has a ~$1.37 trillion market cap, roughly equal to the entire GDP of Australia.' }
