      'You manage a $200,000 portfolio for a 45-year-old planning to retire at 65. Inflation is 5% and rising. The portfolio is currently 60% stocks and 40% bonds. You need to add commodity exposure to hedge inflation while managing risk. Make three strategic decisions.',
