            { label: 'GLD (SPDR Gold Trust), holds 860+ tonnes of physical gold in HSBC London vaults, trades like a stock', consequence: 'Optimal choice. GLD provides physical gold exposure with stock-market liquidity. Each share represents ~1/10th oz of real gold. No storage hassle, no insurance costs, and you can buy/sell in seconds. Expense ratio of 0.40% is the cost of convenience.', score: 3 },
            { label: 'Gold futures contracts for maximum leverage', consequence: 'Futures require active management, margin calls during drawdowns, and understanding of contract rolls. A 45-year-old saving for retirement shouldn\'t be managing leveraged futures positions. One wrong move and margin calls could force selling at the worst time.', score: 0 }
