            { label: 'Rebalance back to your 10% target by trimming commodities and buying beaten-down bonds', consequence: 'Textbook rebalancing. Selling what has surged (commodities at +35%) and buying what has dropped (bonds) is systematically selling high and buying low. This disciplined approach harvests gains from the commodity spike while maintaining your target risk profile.', score: 3 },
            { label: 'Sell all commodities, the spike was a one-time event', consequence: 'Eliminating commodities removes your inflation hedge and crisis protection. Geopolitical tensions can persist for years (Russia-Ukraine). Selling the entire position after one spike means you have zero protection if inflation continues or another crisis hits.', score: 1 }
