      'Commodities serve a specific role in portfolios: inflation hedging and crisis protection. The optimal approach is a permanent 5-10% allocation using efficient vehicles (GLD for gold, broad commodity ETFs or producer stocks for energy/agriculture), with disciplined rebalancing during spikes and crashes. Commodities are not a get-rich-quick trade, they\'re portfolio insurance that pays off when you need it most: during inflation, wars, supply shocks, and financial crises.'
