      'Three critical problems: (1) Performance, the AVERAGE hedge fund returns 7.2% after fees vs 10.3% for a free S&P 500 index fund. Without access to the top 10% of managers, they\'d likely be better off in an index fund. (2) Access, at $60K income and $50K net worth, they almost certainly aren\'t an accredited investor ($200K income or $1M net worth required). Most hedge funds won\'t accept them. (3) Concentration/liquidity, 100% of savings in one illiquid investment violates every rule of personal finance. Hedge funds have lockup periods, and an emergency would leave them unable to access their own money.'
