      ['How does rebalancing improve returns?','Rebalancing systematically sells high (trimming assets that have outperformed) and buys low (adding to assets that have underperformed). This mechanical process adds an estimated 0.5-1% annually to returns over long periods.'],
      ['What is the "modified endowment model" for individual investors?','50% stocks, 20% bonds, 10% REITs/real estate, 10% infrastructure/farmland, 5% commodities/gold, 5% other alternatives. This captures most diversification benefits using liquid, accessible instruments.'],
      ['Why did the 60/40 fail in 2022?','Both stocks (-19%) and bonds (-13%) fell simultaneously when the Fed raised rates to fight inflation. The 60/40 assumes negative stock-bond correlation, which broke down. Alternatives with inflation protection (farmland +18.7%, infrastructure +8-12%) would have helped.']
