        { term: 'Drawdown Recovery', definition: 'The time required for a portfolio to recover from its maximum loss back to its previous peak. Deeper drawdowns require exponentially longer recovery periods.', example: 'A -32% drawdown requires a +47% gain to break even. A -20% drawdown only requires +25%. Alternatives reduce drawdowns, dramatically shortening recovery time.' }
