        'The advisor ignores four decades of evidence: (1) Brinson proved allocation drives 91.5% of returns, adding uncorrelated alternatives improves the efficient frontier. (2) The 60/40 failed in 2022 when stocks and bonds fell together. (3) Farmland (11.5%/yr), infrastructure (10.2%/yr), and real estate (11.4%/yr) have matched or beaten stocks with lower volatility. (4) Liquid ETFs make alternatives as simple as buying an index fund. The modified endowment model captures these benefits with 8 ETFs.',
