      'Designing a growth-oriented modified endowment for the 25-year-old, an income-focused inflation-protected portfolio for the retirees, and a full endowment model for the foundation, scoring 9/9.',
      'The capstone reveals that there is no single "best" portfolio, only the best portfolio FOR EACH CLIENT. The Five Pillars framework is universal, but its application varies: younger investors emphasize growth and accept more risk. Retirees prioritize income and inflation protection with maximum liquidity. Foundations with perpetual horizons maximize illiquidity premium and access. The constant across all three: alternatives improve risk-adjusted returns at every life stage, for every investor type, and in every economic environment. You now have the knowledge to invest more intelligently than 99% of individuals.'
